WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.160
I was on my way home one evening,
quite late at night, on the bus,

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.800
so I wasn't paying much attention
to what was going on around me.

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:07.720
Until I suddenly looked down

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.960
and realised that the man sitting
next to me had his hand on my leg.

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:14.080
He moved his hand upwards
and grabbed me in the crotch.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:17.680
Because I was on the phone
to my mum, I said

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:20.600
'I'm on the bus,
this man just groped me.'

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.080
And everybody on the bus heard me.

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.120
And everybody looked away.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.480
Nobody stepped in.
No-one challenged him.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:45.040
No-one even made
eye contact with me.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.800
And it sent me such
a powerful message.

00:00:46.880 --> 00:00:48.400
It felt like they were saying,

00:00:48.480 --> 00:00:50.760
"We don't want anything to do
with this. This is your thing."

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:53.560
It made me feel that I was at fault,
that I'd done something wrong.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:57.200
I felt incredibly embarrassed
and ashamed and confused,

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.960
and I got off the bus
at the next stop

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:00.600
and walked the rest of the way home.

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:02.680
Looking back,
I wasn't the only person

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.920
who got such a powerful
message that night.

00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.920
So did the man who groped me.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.120
He got the message,
"You can get away with this."

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:11.960
It sent the message that
this was just acceptable.

00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:20.640
We're so used to receiving
the message from all around us

00:01:20.720 --> 00:01:23.720
all the time, that women and girls
are sexual objects.

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.160
That our bodies are public property

00:01:26.240 --> 00:01:29.000
and that we really are the sum
of our individual parts.

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:32.720
There are witchcraft cases
from Europe 400 years ago

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:35.040
where, for example, a woman
was accused of witchcraft

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:37.120
for giving a man a
'permanent erection'.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:40.840
The idea that men couldn't possibly
be expected to control themselves

00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:41.920
is nothing new.

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:44.640
But it's also something that's still
really impacting people's lives,

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:45.760
even today.

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:48.960
Now were you able
to wear undergarments?

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.800
You're like the fifth person
that's asked me that today.

00:01:50.880 --> 00:01:52.560
Well, no, because,
is it inappropriate?

00:01:52.640 --> 00:01:54.240
-To ask somebody what kind
of underpants they wear?

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.360
-I didn't ask you what kind.

00:01:55.680 --> 00:01:57.240
You just asked me
if I was wearing any.

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.440
-Could you?
-No, what do you wear underneath?

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:01.080
What do you wear
underneath something...

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:01.960
Overalls.

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:02.840
-Do you wear clothes?

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:07.160
You wear dungarees. You can't wear
clothes under it it's like a wetsuit.

00:02:07.240 --> 00:02:09.560
-Practically.
-OK, so you answered my question.

00:02:09.640 --> 00:02:12.000
Well I don't know, maybe it's
a little bit more than a wetsuit.

00:02:12.080 --> 00:02:14.800
Was I wearing underwear?
I mean, gosh.

00:02:14.880 --> 00:02:17.280
I think the defensiveness here
is really key.

00:02:17.360 --> 00:02:19.360
This idea that he is
immediately reaching to say,

00:02:19.440 --> 00:02:21.160
"Well I haven't done anything wrong,
you're overreacting."

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:22.880
And that he kind of gets
a little bit of support for that

00:02:22.960 --> 00:02:26.320
from her male co-star, and this
is something that we see a lot of,

00:02:26.400 --> 00:02:29.600
that if women try to challenge
this kind of thing, try to speak out,

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:31.440
often there can be a closing of ranks

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:34.480
in a sense of, "No, no, no, you
don't get to be upset about this."

00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.520
In most British homes,
parents clearly differentiate

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.480
between their sons and daughters.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:41.760
But not in this
north London household.

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:44.080
Here they aim to bring up
their children

00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:46.520
in what they call a non-sexist way.

00:02:47.160 --> 00:02:49.080
I think what's really sad
watching this now

00:02:49.160 --> 00:02:51.360
is that it still feels a
little bit revolutionary.

00:02:51.640 --> 00:02:54.840
Wouldn't be fair for all the girls
to buy princesses

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:58.920
and all the boys
to buy superheroes.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:01.120
Why?

00:03:01.560 --> 00:03:05.840
Because girls want superheroes
and the boys want superheroes.

00:03:05.920 --> 00:03:12.400
And the girls want pink stuff
and the boys don't want pink stuff.

00:03:13.640 --> 00:03:15.160
-Yeah.
-Yeah.

00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:17.520
She makes it sound so simple,
doesn't she?

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:19.760
How is it possible
that this child gets it

00:03:19.840 --> 00:03:23.960
and yet every time a large retailer
agrees to stop gendering its toys

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:27.240
or its children's clothes
as for boys or for girls,

00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:28.520
you'll see a backlash in the press?

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.640
These kinds of stereotypes that
are so insidious and so low-level,

00:03:32.720 --> 00:03:34.840
they are so often dismissed
as not a big deal.

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:37.400
In reality all we're saying is that
kids should have the choice.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:40.280
That, just as she says,
some girls might like princesses

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.120
and some might like superheroes,
but shouldn't they have the option?

00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.160
The reality is that fewer than one
in ten of our engineers is female,

00:03:46.240 --> 00:03:49.080
and our Royal Society, one of our
biggest scientific institutions,

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:50.640
has never had a female president.

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:53.400
So no, of course these things aren't
the end of the world on their own,

00:03:53.480 --> 00:03:56.760
but do they contribute to a world
in which girls are very, very gently

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:59.480
and slowly told, "This isn't for you,
this isn't for you"?

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:03.080
Of course they do, and actually
the end effect is quite extreme.

00:04:03.560 --> 00:04:08.520
Andy, Sam is the first US player to
reach a major semi-final since 2009.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.440
How would you describe--
Male player.

00:04:11.680 --> 00:04:12.480
I beg your pardon?

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:13.680
-Male player, right?
-Yes.

00:04:13.760 --> 00:04:15.800
We are seeing an increasing
number of male role models

00:04:15.880 --> 00:04:17.080
who are choosing to step in

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.640
and just to mention this stuff
when it happens.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:22.160
Not necessarily in a particularly
aggressive or angry way,

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.160
but simply just mentioning it
so that that isn't allowed to stand.

00:04:26.520 --> 00:04:29.480
If you haven't experienced
sexism yourself,

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.440
like with other
forms of prejudice,

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:33.360
it becomes much easier to ignore

00:04:33.440 --> 00:04:35.520
and to deny the reality
of its existence.

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:38.200
It's easy to suggest that
people are overreacting,

00:04:38.280 --> 00:04:39.720
that they must
be making something up,

00:04:39.800 --> 00:04:41.120
because you haven't seen it.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.600
Essentially, the truth is
that we can't change this

00:04:43.680 --> 00:04:46.120
as long as everybody just
thinks it's normal.

